<big>Welcome to Packarch</big>

Packarch is based on CachyOS, itself based on Arch Linux. It keeps what makes CachyOS great (optimized kernels, hardware detection, CachyOS repositories) and adds its own desktops, themes and packages.

<big>Desktops and themes</big>

Packarch provides the Openbox and XFCE desktops. On Openbox, about ten complete themes (wallpaper, polybar bar, colors of the terminal, rofi and notifications, GTK and Openbox themes) are switched in one click from the desktop menu. Fonts are chosen from the menu too (Changer de police) and apply to every theme.

<big>Packages</big>

The packages of Packarch (themes, icons, wallpapers, configuration, applications) come from the [packarch] repository, in addition to the Arch Linux and CachyOS repositories. They are updated with the rest of the system.

<big>Hardware and kernels</big>

Hardware is handled by the CachyOS tools: chwd detects the needed drivers (free or proprietary graphics drivers…) and CachyOS Kernel Manager installs other kernels. The Apps/Tweaks button of this window gives access to these tools and to a few system settings.

<big>Getting help</big>

As Packarch is based on CachyOS and Arch Linux, their documentation almost always applies:

    - <a href="https://wiki.cachyos.org">CachyOS Wiki</a> - official documentation of CachyOS.
    - <a href="https://wiki.archlinux.org">Arch Wiki</a> - the reference documentation of Arch Linux.
    - <a href="https://aur.archlinux.org">AUR</a> - additional software, built from source.

For a problem specific to Packarch (themes, desktops, packages of the [packarch] repository, installation), <a href="https://github.com/Antidote1911/CachyOS-Packarch/issues">report it on GitHub</a>.

We hope that you will enjoy Packarch!
